BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Cookpoint Academy) Tj T* () Tj T* (Cookpoint Academy) Tj T* (Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Many immigrant families and teenagers in our city want to find work but do not know how to get) Tj T* (started. The restaurant industry is one of the biggest employers of immigrants and young) Tj T* (people, and it often has open positions. However, most restaurants require a food-handler) Tj T* (certification, and many want some cooking experience. The people who most need these jobs often) Tj T* (do not have access to affordable training. Community colleges can be far away, and their) Tj T* (classes may be expensive or held at inconvenient times. Language barriers also make it hard to) Tj T* (follow traditional cooking instruction. We believe there is a gap between the people who want) Tj T* (to work in food service and the training that is available to them in their own neighborhoods.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Cookpoint Academy is a neighborhood teaching kitchen that uses connected smart stoves to guide) Tj T* (students through cooking classes. Each stove has a screen that shows the student what to do) Tj T* (next, including the right temperature, how long to cook, and how to handle the food safely.) Tj T* (Because the stove guides the student, the class does not depend entirely on the instructor, and) Tj T* (students can learn at their own pace. The guidance can be shown in several languages, which) Tj T* (helps families who are still learning English. Students attend a series of classes that build) Tj T* (skills step by step. At the end of the series, they prepare for the food-handler certification) Tj T* (exam. After certification, we help connect students with restaurants that are hiring for entry) Tj T* (level positions.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We believe this combination of hardware, curriculum and a local physical space is a new way to) Tj T* (deliver job training. The teaching kitchen also becomes a place where the neighborhood can) Tj T* (gather, which we think will help us build trust with families.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The market for Cookpoint Academy is immigrant families and teenagers who are interested in) Tj T* (working in restaurants. There are many immigrants in our metropolitan area, and a large share) Tj T* (of them work in food service or want to. There are also many teenagers looking for their first) Tj T* (job. If even a small percentage of these people enrolled in our classes, the market would be) Tj T* (large. The restaurant industry is also growing and often reports difficulty finding workers,) Tj T* (which suggests there is demand for trained employees. We have not yet conducted a formal market) Tj T* (study, but we have talked informally with friends and family members who said the idea sounds) Tj T* (interesting. We plan to do more research once we have funding.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Cookpoint Academy will earn revenue in several ways. First, students or their families will pay) Tj T* (a class fee for each series of classes. Second, we hope to receive payments from restaurants) Tj T* (that hire our graduates, similar to a recruiting fee. Third, we may apply for grants from) Tj T* (workforce development programs and foundations. Fourth, we may eventually sell or lease our) Tj T* (smart stove system to other training programs and schools. We have not yet decided on exact) Tj T* (prices. Because our target students may have limited income, we expect to keep class fees low,) Tj T* (and we believe that grants and restaurant payments can make up the difference. The smart stoves) Tj T* (are a significant cost, but we believe they will pay for themselves over time because they) Tj T* (allow us to run more classes with fewer instructors.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our competitors include community college culinary programs, nonprofit job training) Tj T* (organizations, and online cooking videos and courses. Community colleges offer more advanced) Tj T* (training but are often expensive and far from the neighborhoods we serve. Nonprofits offer) Tj ET
endstream
