BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (valuable programs, but many have long waiting lists and limited space. Online courses are cheap) Tj T* (but do not give students hands-on practice or help with finding jobs. We believe Cookpoint) Tj T* (Academy is different because we combine hands-on cooking with smart technology and job) Tj T* (placement in one local place. We do not believe any other organization in our area offers) Tj T* (exactly this combination. We recognize that larger organizations could copy our approach, but) Tj T* (we think our local relationships will give us an advantage.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marisol Echeverria-Tran is our chief executive. She is a business major at our university and) Tj T* (has worked part time in restaurants for three years. She leads strategy, partnerships and) Tj T* (fundraising.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Dwayne Okonkwo-Hale is our chief technology officer. He is a computer engineering student who) Tj T* (designed and built our prototype smart stove guidance system. He leads hardware and software) Tj T* (development.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Priyanka Venkataraghavan is our head of programs. She is studying education and nutrition and) Tj T* (is responsible for designing the class curriculum and preparing students for certification.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We do not yet have a professional chef on the team, but we plan to hire or partner with one. We) Tj T* (also plan to recruit advisors from the restaurant industry and from workforce development) Tj T* (organizations.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined our core business concept and formed a legal entity as an S Corp. Dwayne) Tj T* (has built a first prototype of the smart stove guidance system, which displays steps and timers) Tj T* (on a screen connected to a single stove. We have tested the prototype with a small group of) Tj T* (friends, who said it was easy to use. We have not yet run a real class, signed up any students,) Tj T* (or partnered with any restaurants. We do not yet have a website.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our financial plan is still early. We estimate that opening our first teaching kitchen will) Tj T* (require a space to rent, several smart stoves, kitchen equipment, insurance, and money to pay) Tj T* (instructors. We believe the total startup cost will be significant, though we have not yet) Tj T* (prepared a detailed budget. We do not currently have revenue. We have personally contributed a) Tj T* (small amount of money to form the company and build the prototype. Over the next two years, we) Tj T* (hope to open one kitchen, enroll a few hundred students, and reach break-even, although we have) Tj T* (not yet built a projection to show how this will happen.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are asking for prize funding from this competition to help us rent a space and buy the first) Tj T* (set of smart stoves and kitchen equipment. We would also welcome mentorship from judges and) Tj T* (advisors with experience in restaurants, education, and hardware. In particular, we would like) Tj T* (help with building a detailed budget, understanding food safety regulations, and finding) Tj T* (restaurants willing to hire our graduates. We would also appreciate introductions to local) Tj T* (community organizations and grant programs. We believe that with the support of this) Tj T* (competition, Cookpoint Academy can begin to help immigrant families and teenagers build careers) Tj T* (in food service, while building a company that grows over time.) Tj ET
endstream
